        </p>
        <p>
          The <strong>Commercial Continuous Supercritical CO2 Static-Mixer Micro-Encapsulation (scCO2-SME)</strong> platform operates at mild physiological temperatures (35–42°C) without organic solvents by leveraging supercritical carbon dioxide (critical point: T_c = 31.1°C, P_c = 73.8 bar) as a green plasticizer, anti-solvent, and atomization driver through four coupled thermodynamic principles:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-muted">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink">Dense-Phase Dissolution &amp; Interfacial Tension Collapse:</strong> At pressures between 100 and 320 bar, supercritical CO2 dissolves into lipid carriers and biopolymer matrices, dropping dynamic viscosity by 85–95% and lowering interfacial tension &gamma; by orders of magnitude via high-density gas saturation (PGSS mechanism).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink">Laminar/Turbulent Static Mixer Striation:</strong> Passing through high-intensity static mixer geometries (e.g., Sulzer SMX Plus cross-bars or Kenics helical elements) creates a localized shear field (&gamma;&#775; = 25,000–65,000 s<sup>−1</sup>). The alternating X-grids continuously divide, stretch, and reorient fluid lamellae, reducing striation thickness to sub-micron dimensions (&lt;0.18 &mu;m) and producing a hyper-homogeneous emulsion of active core droplets within the plasticized shell biopolymer.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink">Instantaneous Decompression &amp; Nucleation (RESS/PGSS):</strong> Expanding the pressurized gas-saturated solution through a precision laser-drilled coaxial micro-orifice (120–180 &mu;m) at rates exceeding 10<sup>7</sup> bar/s induces instantaneous CO2 supersaturation and flashing from dense fluid to gas. The sudden volumetric expansion breaks the liquid jet into monodisperse micro-droplets (Sauter mean diameter d<sub>32</sub> = 180–450 nm), while CO2 desolvation triggers instantaneous precipitation and solid shell crystallization around the core payload.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ink">Anti-Freeze Active Induction Thermal Compensation:</strong> Rapid gas decompression causes extreme Joule-Thomson cooling (&Delta;T<sub>JT</sub> = &mu;<sub>JT</sub> &Delta;P). To prevent solid dry ice crystallization and capillary nozzle freeze-choking, an integrated coaxial induction heating collar maintains the nozzle tip at +45 to +55°C, ensuring steady supersonic atomization and 100% operational uptime.
